From df205614add4e3dcf29147319943a6ccf226d01d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:52:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test: match structured logs and fail functionals on dropped
 records

Keep substring matching and a human text log while adding a JSON sidecar and nested typed field matching. Drain live-node logging at assertion boundaries, track changed log paths, and handle JSON-only nodes. A worker-written final counter makes dropped records an explicit functional failure rather than a missing-log timeout.

Validated the exact framework plus bounded-load candidate tree e61b616721b358d0d9336b41a2b52ae51b4475e5: full extended suite 276 passed, 61 platform/disabled skips, zero failures, 764.8 seconds. Source and executable hashes stayed fixed. Native logging/event/metrics/RPC checks: 66 cases, 393755 assertions. Collector and production call-site changes are separate.

(cherry picked from commit 554ecf419218f2efc3b787570ed04bbb3e6a9d2c)

